.SH "NAME"
.PP
\fIroot\fP \- override the global root

.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP
This handler allows for overriding the \fB\fCroot\fR directive from the global block in the current handler block.
It works identical to the atomdns\-global(1) \fB\fCroot\fR's configuration.

.SH "SYNTAX"
.PP
.RS

.nf
root DIRECTORY

.fi
.RE

.IP \(bu 4
with \fB\fCroot\fR \fBDIRECTORY\fP is the directory to use as the root directory in the handler block. Any relative path
names will get this directory prefixed. If \fBDIRECTORY\fP itself is also relative, the current working
directory (cwd) of the atomdns process will be prefixed.


.SH "EXAMPLES"
.PP
.RS

.nf
example.org {
    root /my/zones
    dbfile db.example.org
}

.fi
.RE

.PP
The "db.example.org" zone should now be located in /my/zones.

.SH "NOTES"
.PP
This handler must be set first in a handler block to effect all subsequent handlers in the block.

.SH "ALSO SEE"
.PP
atomdns\-global(1).
